{"step_index":6459,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T10:52:19Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-24T13:52:19+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-24T13:52:19+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///D:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/server_manager.py`\nTotal Lines: 359\nTotal Bytes: 13739\nShowing lines 120 to 180\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n120:             self.log(f\"Server process started successfully (PID: {self.process.pid}).\")\n121:             return {\"success\": True, \"message\": \"started\", \"pid\": self.process.pid, \"port\": self.port}\n122:         except Exception as e:\n123:             self.log(f\"Failed to start server: {e}\")\n124:             return {\"success\": False, \"message\": str(e)}\n125: \n126:     def stop(self) -> dict:\n127:         try:\n128:             self.log(\"Stopping server...\")\n129:             \n130:             # Step 1: Call graceful /shutdown endpoint\n131:             try:\n132:                 requests.get(f\"http://127.0.0.1:{self.port}/shutdown\", timeout=1.5)\n133:             except Exception:\n134:                 pass\n135: \n136:             # Wait briefly for port to release\n137:             for _ in range(8):\n138:                 if not is_port_listening(self.port):\n139:                     break\n140:                 time.sleep(0.15)\n141: \n142:             # Step 2: Terminate tracked process if still alive\n143:             if self.process is not None:\n144:                 try:\n145:                     if os.name == 'nt':\n146:                         subprocess.run(['taskkill', '/F', '/T', '/PID', str(self.process.pid)], capture_output=True)\n147:                     else:\n148:                         os.killpg(os.getpgid(self.process.pid), signal.SIGTERM)\n149: